<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaman Shah Durrani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1793">1793</a>–<a href="/years/1801">1801</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Zaman Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zaman Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani</a> was ruler of the Durrani Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> in the 1790s, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a>. He launched several invasions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> exploited Zaman Shah's withdrawal from the Punjab in 1799 to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a>, beginning his consolidation of power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaman-shah-durrani.jpg" alt="Zaman Shah Durrani" width="283" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Zaman_Shah_Durrani_of_Afghanistan-cropped-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>That balance was later upset by his grandson <b>Zaman Shah</b>, who replaced Barakzai leaders with men of his own Sadozai lineage.</blockquote><a href="/empire/durrani-empire">Durrani Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Ranjit Singh's consolidation began when, aged only eighteen, he exploited the withdrawal of the Durrani ruler <b>Zaman Shah</b> from the Punjab to seize Lahore from its Bhangi chiefs in July 1799, with the support of his formidable mother-in-law Sada Kaur of the Kanhaiya Misl.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirhind">Sirhind-Fategarh</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=31.62,65.72&amp;year=1797" aria-label="Kandahar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6245 1012 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Zaman Shah Durrani"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6695 1282h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6695 1282h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=31.62,65.72&amp;year=1797">What was here in 1797? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
